  "reason": "Evidence: config_032 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, transformer, concat) is our best result at 0.688 acc, only ~0.035 above the best RNA-only (config_006, 0.653). We have no data on fusion strategy—concat is the only method tested. Question: Does weighted fusion outperform simple concatenation for combining the scvi_n200 RNA features with ResNet50 image features? config_033 changes only the fusion method (concat→weighted) relative to config_032, making it a clean single-variable comparison. Why this is the best next experiment: It directly tests an important, unexplored design axis (fusion) with minimal confounding. If weighted fusion helps, it reveals that modality interaction is a meaningful lever; if it does not, we can rule out fusion as a bottleneck and redirect effort toward image encoder quality (ViT-L) or RNA-side improvements. Under a limited budget, this controlled 1-variable test maximizes information per experiment."
}

